From: nxrs contributors
Subject: [PATCH RFC] Xtensa: branch directly on single-bit integer tests

Select BBCI/BBSI for branch-only equality/inequality of one masked bit.
Combine before large masks become literal-pool loads; retain multi-bit,
shared-value and Boolean-result lowering. No application change or CPU
feature flag is required: these are core Xtensa instructions.

Complete their branch metadata, analysis, inversion, range checking,
insertion and constant-island relaxation before enabling selection. Tests
cover both polarities, small/large masks, shared values, distinct predicates,
far targets and native verified objects on generic, ESP32 and ESP32-S3.
Refresh the existing byte-mask test without changing its IR or RUN command.

This extends the sign-mask evaluation chain, excludes 0019, and remains an
inactive RFC. Device profitability and broader qualification are separate.

